# {{.Slug}}

Stripe webhook consumer. Verifies `Stripe-Signature` at the receiver
(reactor built-in), then routes on `event.type`.

Generated by `reactor new stripe-webhook {{.Slug}}` on {{.Date}}.

## Prerequisites

Add a vault credential named `fulfilment-api-key` (or rename in main.go)
holding the bearer for your fulfilment service:

```bash
reactor vault add --name fulfilment-api-key --service fulfilment \
  --provider shared-secret --value $FULFILMENT_BEARER --auto-rotate=false
reactor vault grant --workflow {{.Slug}} --credential fulfilment-api-key
```

## Run it locally

```bash
reactor workflow build --src . --slug {{.Slug}}
reactor workflow register --db sqlite://./reactor.db --slug {{.Slug}} --src main.go
reactor serve --db sqlite://./reactor.db
```

In the dashboard at <http://127.0.0.1:7777/workflows/{{.Slug}}>, click
"Add webhook trigger" with provider `stripe`. The redirect flashes the
URL + secret one time; paste both into Stripe's webhook endpoint config.

## Extend

Each handler is its own Step with an idempotency key derived from the
event id, so Stripe's automatic retries on transient failures are safe.
Add a `case` for any other Stripe event type you need.
